## Mechanical backstop

Both adapters (`.claude/hooks/check_commit_msg.py` and
`.agents/hooks/check_commit_msg.py`) symlink to the same shared
implementation, wired via each adapter's `commit-msg` hook, which itself
symlinks to `.git/hooks/commit-msg` — warn-only, exits 0 always, exempts
merges and `fixup!`/`squash!` commits; anything not matching a role prefix
is simply flagged, never rejected. `ROLE_PREFIX_RE` matches: Planner, Coder,
Runner, Reviewer, Author, Researcher.

## Remote

`origin` → `[SET AT SETUP: VCS_REMOTE]` (SSH, private repo). Commits happen
at Reviewer close-out per above; pushing to `origin` is a separate, visible
action — confirm with the user before pushing unless a given session has
already authorized it for that pass.
